@startuml lockfree-epoch-reclamation
' ============================================================================
' lockfree-epoch-reclamation.puml — a pinned reader and a CAS-ing writer run
' concurrently. The reader pins an epoch and reads the old node safely; the
' writer swaps the root and QUEUES the old node, but the epoch cannot advance
' (and the node cannot be freed) until every reader pinned to that epoch exits.
' This is what closes the ABA / use-after-free window.
' Source: §Epoch-Based Reclamation of lockfree-cas-artrie.md.
' Color key (house palette):
'   green  #2E7D32  the reader's safe (pinned) window / the safe free
'   red    #C62828  the deferred-until-quiescent reclamation
'   slate  border   the epoch manager lifeline
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam participantBorderColor #37474F
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam noteBorderColor #90A4AE

title Epoch reclamation — free the old node only after every pinned reader leaves

participant "Reader\n(A)" as RD
participant "Epoch\nmgr" as EP #CFD8DC
participant "Writer\n(B)" as WR

RD -> EP : enter_read()\npin epoch e
activate RD
note left of RD #C8E6C9 : reads OLD node\nsafely while\npinned to e

WR -> WR : CAS root\nold → new
WR -> EP : retire(old)\ninto epoch e
note right of WR #FFCDD2 : old node is\nUNLINKED but\nNOT yet freed

RD -> EP : exit_read()\nunpin e
deactivate RD

WR -> EP : try advance epoch
EP -[#2E7D32]-> WR : e quiescent →\nfree old node
note over EP #C8E6C9 : reclaim runs only\nonce e drains:\nno UAF, no ABA
@enduml
